PCIIDS.DAT is made by tools/mkpciids.py from the PCI ID Project's list of PCI IDs (pci.ids;
https://pci-ids.ucw.cz/), maintained by Albert Pool, Martin Mares and other volunteers. The list may be
distributed under either the GNU General Public License (version 2 or higher) or the 3-clause BSD License;
GLOS uses it under the 3-clause BSD License, below. PCIIDS.DAT holds the list's vendors and devices (no
subsystems, no classes) and its header's lines, packed with deflate. The source: github.com/pciutils/pciids
commit bc2920f3fc38e42d0aecc8ce4b17d1ed034dbd70 (list version 2026.11.21), pci.ids sha256
39f98c0574bbb7d3a4e90899e43b324ae9d511222381691372bdbb27e7df11d8.

